{"content": "Writes effective and clear texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "terrace", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a flat area next to a building where people can sit and relax", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Historians wrote about these \"hanging\" gardens, which were planted on a series of terraces supported by columns by ancient Babylonians. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when you write about history and civilizations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "astonishing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "causing a feeling of great surprise or wonder ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It must have been an astonishing sight!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "array", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large group or number of things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nebuchadnezzar is known to have ordered the construction of a vast array of buildings.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to console ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to try to make someone feel less sadness or disappointment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Tradition has it that the gardens were created by the king to console his wife, who missed her homeland.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "oasis", "type": "name"}, {"content": " an area in a desert where there is water and plants", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Although Babylon rarely received rain, the gardens were lush and provided an oasis in the desert landscape.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to irrigate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to supply something, such as land, with water by artificial means ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Even with the absence of  modern engines and water pumps at such an early date, the gardens were constantly irrigated with the water from the Euphrates River.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to erect", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to build something by putting together materials", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Made of bronze, the statue of the sun god Helios was erected by the citizens near the harbor of their island in about 280 BC ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le08ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbial Clauses of Contrast ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">adverbial clauses</span> of contrast in your writing to show that the actions you are writing about are not expected.  </br> Using clauses of this nature makes your writing more sophisticated and easier to read.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbial clauses</span> of contrast refer to a concession (where you compromise)  or when the result is unanticipated or unforeseen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The clauses are introduced by the conjunctions <span class=\"italic\">although, even though, though, whereas, despite, in spite of </span>or <span class=\"italic\">while.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Although Babylon rarely received rain</span>, the gardens were lush and provided an oasis in the desert landscape. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " These types of clauses are <span class=\"underline\">dependent</span> - meaning they cannot stand alone. They need to be attached to the main clause. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Even though</span> there were no modern engines or water pumps at such an early date, the gardens were constantly irrigated with the water from the Euphrates River.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Despite </span>being one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World, the Colossus of Rhodes is often overlooked.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">In spite of</span> its destruction, historians and tourists alike still admire this majestic work of art.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Although</span> the Colossus collapsed during an earthquake in 225 BC the pieces lay untouched where they had fallen for hundreds of years.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past </span>to talk about finished events at a particular time in the past.</br>  You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Simple Past</span> <span class=\"underline\">passive</span> when you want to focus on the action that is done to the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You form the <span class=\"underline\">passive</span> by using <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">was/were</span> + past participle</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The doer or agent of the action is either not known or not mentioned as the receiver of the action is more important to the context.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:</br><span class=\"italic\">  Historians wrote about these \"hanging\" gardens, which <span class=\"strong\">were planted</span> on a series of terraces supported by columns.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes you use the preposition 'by' to mention the person or thing that did the action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:  </br><span class=\"italic\">Some believe that the gardens <span class=\"strong\">were built by</span> the king in about 600 BC in an area that is now southern Iraq. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The amazing \"hanging\" gardens were planted on  terraces so the vegetation spilled down.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They were built in a dry area, which made them even more wonderful to see. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Tradition has it that the gardens were created by the king to console his wife, who missed her homeland. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research ancient civilizations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use my notes to write a paragraph about an ancient wonder.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use the Passive form to talk about facts and events.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online or to a local library and look for information about another ancient wonder.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the information from 3 different sites or books and take notes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compile the information and write a 120-150 word paragraph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the Passive form to talk about facts and events.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your paragraph.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your paragraph to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "content